.TH SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DEVICE_STREAM_ROLE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DEVICE_STREAM_ROLE \- Specify an application role for an audio device.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DEVICE_STREAM_ROLE \(dqSDL_AUDIO_DEVICE_STREAM_ROLE\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Some audio backends (such as Pipewire) allow you to describe the role of your audio stream\[char46] Among other things, this description might show up in a system control panel or software for displaying and manipulating media playback/recording graphs\[char46]
.PP
This hints lets you transmit that information to the OS\[char46] The contents of this hint are used while opening an audio device\[char46] You should use a string that describes your what your program is playing (Game, Music, Movie, etc\[char46]\[char46]\[char46])\[char46]
.PP
Setting this to \(dq\(dq or leaving it unset will have SDL use a reasonable default: \(dqGame\(dq or something similar\[char46]
.PP
Note that while this talks about audio streams, this is an OS-level concept, so it applies to a physical audio device in this case, and not an
.BR SDL_AudioStream ,
nor an SDL logical audio device\[char46]
.PP
For Windows WASAPI audio, the following roles are supported, and map to
.BR AUDIO_STREAM_CATEGORY :
.PP

\(bu \(dqOther\(dq (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dqCommunications\(dq - Real-time communications, such as VOIP or chat
.PP
\(bu \(dqGame\(dq - Game audio
.PP
\(bu \(dqGameChat\(dq - Game chat audio, similar to \(dqCommunications\(dq except that this will not attenuate other audio streams
.PP
\(bu \(dqMovie\(dq - Music or sound with dialog
.PP
\(bu \(dqMedia\(dq - Music or sound without dialog
.PP
Android\(aqs AAudio target supports this hint as of SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]4\[char46] Android does not support the exact same options as WASAPI, but for portability, will attempt to map these same strings to the
.BR aaudio_usage_t
constants\[char46] For example, \(dqMovie\(dq and \(dqMedia\(dq will both map to
.BR AAUDIO_USAGE_MEDIA ,
etc\[char46]
.PP
If your application applies its own echo cancellation, gain control, and noise reduction it should also set
.BR SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DEVICE_RAW_STREAM \[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before an audio device is opened\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

